cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use encoding3d, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "encoding3d: an exchange format for functional-structural plant model scenes"
abstract: >-
  encoding3d is an exchange format for whole functional-structural plant model (FSPM) scenes, across platforms and
  languages (openalea.metafspm, CPlantBox, GroIMP, VirtualPlantLab), based on glTF 2.0. Each time step is one glTF
  file holding the multiscale plant graphs, their state variables and parameters, their geometry and the
  environment's grids, with one shared vocabulary of variables; sequences of frames, shared parts and instances,
  and archives describe a whole simulation. It also runs models of several platforms together, step by step
  (coupling sessions over ZeroMQ or a folder). The repository holds the specification, its JSON schemas and
  vocabulary, conformance files, a Python reference codec and validator, C++, Java and Julia codecs, and a
  ParaView reader.
